
ELECTRON IMPACT IONIZATION OF HYDROGEN 
ELECTRON RECOMBINATION OF HYDROGEN

Data are taken directly from two DEGAS-format files: ehr1.dat and ehr2.dat.
Both were generated by versions of the Weisheit code, irls. Revisions
made to the code by Daren Stotler have been recorded in the CVS archive
"collrad". 

  --Version 2.0--
The file ehr1.dat corresponds to the file fort.18 in the repository,
revision 1.1. The generating code (and the data file) have the tag
r1_5. Relative to the original Weisheit code, this version has changes
made by Detlev Reiter to remove the steady-state assumption of recombination
equalling ionization. It also has Stotler's improvements to the "coupling
to continuum" contributions and energy exchange in recombination. This
file has also been widely used with the old DEGAS code. 

  --Version 2.1--
The file ehr2.dat is the latest version of the file, revision 1.12,
tag r1_13. The difference relative to ehr1.dat is the usage of the
Janev-Smith cross sections in the Weisheit code.

Both files have been altered slightly relative to the code-generated
versions, mainly by replacing ionization rates < 1.e-100 with 1.e-99.

HYDROGEN CHARGE EXCHANGE

  --Version 2.0--
These data were generated by ratecalc, revision 1.26, using hchex.input, 
revision 1.1, as the input file. The cross section values were computed 
from the fit proposed in the Janev-Smith hydrogen database. The reaction
rate and the n=1 moment were integrated by ratecalc using this cross 
section fit in the integrand. The maximum sigma-v value was obtained by
examination from a plot of the cross section.
  --Version 2.1--
Added n=2 moment to the file. Still computed using hchex.input, revision
1.2.

MOLECULAR HYDROGEN DISSOCIATION

  --Version 2.0--
The file itself was generated by ratecalc, revision 1.26, using h2h2p.input,
revision 1.1 as the input file. The reaction rate data should be coming
from the Janev book and the associated Aladdin data, but it turns out that
the fit data for this reaction are incorrect. Instead, the numerical
values of the rates have just been pasted in from the DEGAS file, atmc.dat.
The dissociation energy and electron energy loss have been taken
directly from the Janev book.

MOLECULAR HYDROGEN IONIZATION

  --Version 2.0--
The file itself was generated by ratecalc, revision 1.26, using h2h2p.input,
revision 1.1 as the input file. The reaction rate data are taken
from the Janev book and the associated Aladdin data. Because of 
restrictions on the fit, the first and last four values come out
0. Paste in their values from the DEGAS file, atmc.dat. Note that the
relevant scalar here is the ionization energy, which is taken directly
from the Janev book.

MOLECULAR HYDROGEN DISSOCIATIVE IONIZATION

  --Version 2.0--
The file itself was generated by ratecalc, revision 1.26, using h2dision.input,
revision 1.1 as the input file. The reaction rate data are taken
from the Janev book and the associated Aladdin data. Because of 
restrictions on the fit, the first six and last four values come out
0. Paste in their values from the DEGAS file, atmc.dat. The dissociation
energy and electron energy loss values represent a linear fit to the
temperature dependent prescription given in the Janev book. 
Note that the latter is correct regardless of the energy of the
second electron since said energy remains within the electron fluid.

